content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal leakage is approximately one drop per second. No numerical allowable seal-leak rate is documented. Applying the manual symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal,' the required corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check; the drip rate must not be treated as acceptable merely because no numerical limit is given. Confirm that the leakage is at the shaft seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Applying Figure 3's HF-300 vibration criteria, 3.4 mm/s lies between 2.8 and 4.5 mm/s RMS and therefore falls in Zone B, 'Long-term operation,' provided the report value is RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing. It is below the Zone C range of 4.5–7.1 ('Restricted - plan maintenance') and the Zone D range of 7.1–11.0 ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). The reading is not on a zone boundary.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The vibration procedure requires weekly measurement on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading. The single reported value therefore establishes Zone B only for that reading; readings from both housings and confirmation of the RMS measurement basis are still required.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the reported 'housing 70 C' is bearing-housing temperature, the applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. Thus 70 C is at the upper end of the documented normal range and below both alarm and trip; this reading alone does not require a temperature trip or establish bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The basis for planned P2 repair without an immediate condition-based stop is active seal leakage requiring corrective work, while the reported vibration is in the long-term-operation zone and the reported temperature has not reached alarm or trip. No site priority definitions or allowable run time with the active leak are supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely is a failed or failing mechanical seal, including worn or cracked seal faces. In addition, SB-2026-014 reports early HF3-450 component-seal failures caused by a revised sleeve tolerance on pumps from serial HF3-22000; P-104's serial HF3-22871 is in that affected range. Confirm which seal is actually installed during removal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a documented cause of shaft-seal leakage and is also a possible cause of elevated vibration, making it a common cause to check before return to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry, which is another documented cause of shaft-seal leakage. The pump uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry; flush arrangement and dry-running history need verification.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented explanations for the vibration include bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, cavitation and misalignment. The Zone B reading alone does not distinguish among them; inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH rather than automatically replacing bearings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, verify the leak location and identify the installed seal if externally possible. Confirm that the 3.4 mm/s reading is RMS velocity on a bearing housing, measure both bearing housings, retain the highest value for Figure 3 classification, and confirm the location of the 70 C temperature measurement.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Arrange lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly before removal.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly, remove the impeller nut and impeller, and withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve following the mechanical-seal replacement procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring depth exceeds 0.1 mm. Also inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH for the vibration investigation; replace both bearings as a pair only if inspection finds wear, noise or high temperature, not solely from the current 3.4 mm/s and 70 C readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not fit HF3-450. Fit one new cartridge seal HF3-450B and one new HF3-120 casing gasket. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal installation; this does not remove the separate requirement to inspect sleeve scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the manual Table 5 fasteners on lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. For the HF3-450B seal gland nuts, use the bulletin torque of 30 Nm, not the superseded manual value of 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and complete the alignment check called for by the seal-leakage troubleshooting action. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, restore the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and ensure the pump cannot be run dry. After reassembly, check for recurrent shaft-seal leakage, record bearing-housing temperature, measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading with Figure 3; no numerical post-repair seal-drip acceptance limit is documented.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; mandatory replacement type for this serial range. Do not substitute HF3-450. Gland-nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; install new because the casing/back pull-out assembly is opened and the seal procedure requires a new casing gasket.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional replacement: quantity one only if inspection finds scoring deeper than 0.1 mm; otherwise reuse is not prohibited by the supplied evidence.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting mechanical-seal disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry, including during return to service after seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If conditions worsen before or during return to service, apply the documented limits: Figure 3 identifies Zone D, 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, as 'Damage likely - stop the pump'; bearing-housing temperature alarm is 80 C and trip is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard labour time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour time 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours; include this for the planned alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement, only if inspection establishes wear, noise or high temperature: standard labour time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians. This is not included in the base seal-and-alignment labour allowance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The bulletin was issued 14 March 2026 and specifically applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-104 is HF3-22871, so the serial-specific bulletin applies: use 30 Nm. Pumps below HF3-22000 remain on the manual instructions.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the general manual parts list identifies HF3-450, but the bulletin prohibits fitting HF3-450 on this serial range and requires HF3-450B. Therefore HF3-450B governs for P-104. The previous-shift note claiming that 25 Nm is correct for all pumps and that the bulletin should be ignored is not applicable and must not be followed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 3.4 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what are the current readings on both bearing housings? These details are needed to apply the highest-reading rule conclusively (C06, C07).",
    "Is the reported 70 C specifically bearing-housing temperature? The supplied temperature limits apply to the bearing housing; no limit for another housing location is provided (C02).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, is the drip confirmed to be at the shaft seal, and what is the measured sleeve-scoring depth? These determine whether the reported HF3-450 early-failure mode is directly applicable and whether HF3-455 is required (C09, C13).",
    "What are the alignment, bearing, impeller and NPSH inspection results? The evidence lists possible causes but does not establish the cause of the 3.4 mm/s vibration or justify automatic bearing replacement (C09, C10).",
    "Was there any dry-running or loss of Plan 11 flush? This is needed to assess the documented run-dry seal-failure possibility (C02, C09).",
    "The evidence gives no permissible seal-drip rate, maximum run time before repair, post-repair leakage acceptance criterion or definitions for P1/P2/P3 priorities. Site/operations criteria are required for any continued run-to-repair decision and final leak acceptance (C09)."
  ]
}
